From ad2c6075c80a55a58e6b9422d2c726daf8dda66d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HampterDev <131729366+HampterDev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 00:00:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Return no window for a name-plate lookup without plates

ui_window_mgr_get_window(0x12d) returns the first party name plate, but
when there is no plate it returns the cash-shop window. The 2022-04-06
executable does the same: its jump table sends 0x12d into the code for
0x13e, as if a break were missing. The cash shop is never a name plate,
and a generic ui_window_mgr_post_quit1(0x12d) would then quit the cash
shop while cash_shop_wnd still points to it. No current caller looks up
0x12d, since plate menus find their owner through
ui_window_mgr_find_by_key, so current behavior is unchanged.

Return NULL when there is no plate.

Validation: the new test_name_plate_lookup runs the extracted lookup with
and without plates and with and without an open cash shop; it fails
without the fix. Release build without warnings; the full behavioral
suite passed on the completed series.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VaQB81YtRGLtH8zvfX7WTY
